    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Typical carcinoid",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "A 45-year-old man with multiple endocrine neoplasia type&nbsp;1 had separate primary typical carcinoids in his stomach&nbsp;(<strong>A,B</strong>) and thymus&nbsp;(<strong>D,E</strong>). Both tumours showed strong chromogranin staining&nbsp;(<strong>C</strong>) and low/moderate Ki-67 labelling&nbsp;(<strong>F</strong>).",
    "source": "Philipp Ströbel",
